CONTENT NOTICE
The software code (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) is licensed under MIT above.

The Mahābhārata text, Sanskrit verses, and story content reproduced in this
application are derived from ancient works in the public domain, including:

  - The Mahābhārata (Sanskrit original, ~400 BCE – 400 CE)
    Compiler: Sage Vyāsa (Krishnadvaipāyana)

  - K.M. Ganguli English translation (1883–1896) — public domain
    Published by Pratap Chandra Roy, Calcutta

  - The Bhagavad Gītā (Sanskrit original) — public domain

  - Monier-Williams Sanskrit-English Dictionary (1899) — public domain

These ancient texts are part of humanity's shared cultural and spiritual
heritage and are not subject to copyright. Modern scholarly translations
cited in the app (Wisdomlib, BORI Critical Edition) are used for reference
only; no substantial portions are reproduced.

The web application code itself is original work and is freely licensed
under MIT. Attribution appreciated but not required.
